Have you set the correct system information in the Multia's ARC Console?

You will need  to tell the Multia where the linload.exe file resides, which
should in be the /milo partition.

You do that with the SYSTEMPARTITION, OSLOADER, OSLOADERPARTITION, and
OSLOADFILENAME commands.

they need to be something like:

LOADIDENTIFIER =Linux
SYSTEMPARTITION=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)
OSLADER=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)\linload.exe
OSLOADERPARTITION=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)
OSLOADFILENAME=\milo
OSLOADPARTITIONOPTIONS=boot sda2:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda2

I had to change the partition(X) fields to something like partition(5) since
my /milo partition was on sda6

I had to play with these settings to get mine to work, but it eventually did
work.  There is a little test utility in the ARC Console that will allow you
to check the status of your paritions (or something similiar);  this was a
huge help to me.

hope that helps.

Jon


