Beetle (no_spam_beetle168@hotmail.com) wrote:
: I got my Linux running on my UDB. However, I could not config the sound card
: to work. Another question is regarding the PCMCIA slots. Can I plug in and
: PCMCIA NIC like 3COM in the slot and make Linux recognize the cards?


The multia built in sound stuff is a wss/mss at io address 0x530,
hardwired to interrupt 9 and dma 3. it should also be able to use
dma2=1 but this is screwed up in the kernel sound stuff... 
If you set dma2=1 the config will end up with both dma and dma2 both
equal to 1, which won't work. just use dma=3 with no dma2 
(defaults to -1 (disabled) in newer kernels)

As far as the pcmcia slots, I am unaware of anyone having that stuff
working... I know that it was being tinkered with by some netbsd
folks at one time, but I have no idea if anyone at all has it working on
the multia.

: Thnaks.






