Last week I had exactly the same problems when I tried to install
rh5.2 on my alpha PC from Vobis. Sorry can't give a solution because I
finally gave up. I asked on the axp-list mailing list, and the only
hints I got were,

- try eb164 or pc164. One of those 2 possibilites seemed to work for
some people. For me there wasn't any difference.

- wait a little longer - it just *seems* to be frozen. The suggestion
was to wait at least 30 minutes. Well, I waited 75 minutes, and there
wasn't any sign of life.

- maybe your RAM is not the right one for your alpha, or it just is
bad. Well, I didn't change my RAM in the meantime. Btw., my fine
running and very busy alpha with rh5.0 doesn't give any clue for a bad
RAM.

Again and again people write about "random freezes" during rh5.2
installation. I want to stress that *my* freezes are *not* randomly.
Freezes always occur at the same point, i.e. during installation of
the rh5.2 glibc rpm.


