>
> I've looked everywhere and asked everywhere that I can think of...but
> nobody seems to be able to point me in the right direction...
>
> Does anyone know where I can get the pinout for the debug monitor port
> on my AlphaPC64-275 (cabriolet) motherboard?  I need to reload my
> flashrom--my Alpha has turned into a very expensive doorstop!

There is a row of jumpers at corner of board farthest (diagonal) from power
connectors. One is labeled SP6, put a jumper there. It will not trap to the
SROM Debug port. You will need to now attach a computer via its serial port
to the onboard debug monitor port on the Cabriolet motherboard. This is a LAT
style RJ45 serial connector, you can either mangle a regular RJ45 to remove
the lock tab and ghuide (to make it fit) or you can get a genuine connector
from DEC/Compaq service and parts.

If you need further instructions, contact us and we will point you in the
right direction for the full manual from Digital/Compaq website. You will
also need to get some ROM inages and other files to reinstall your BIOS.

Best regards,

