In article <78k2k1$1ns$1@nntp1.interworld.net>,
  jlawson@orion.ac.hmc.edu (Jeffrey A. Lawson) wrote:
>
> I have been running RedHat 5.2 on my multia for several weeks now, but
> when I have tried to boot one of the 2.2.0-pre and even the final
> 2.2.0 that was released this week, my machine simply hangs after the
> unzipping process.  The last thing I see is the row of hyphens after
> the "turning on virtual addressing and jumping to the Linux kernel"
> message.

This sounds like you built ordinary Intel-style support for VGA console,
instead of TGA support, which the Multia and older AlphaStations want.	The
TGA device is not VGA compatible, and won't show console output.  Just add
the TGA support to your configuration.

In the 2.0.xx kernels, you had to "make config" in order to get to these
options.  I don't no if the final 2.2 has fixed menuconfig (word is this is
much improved, with sparc and alpha archs getting same support as Intel
here.)

You might also try building FBCon support, with the TGA device.  This is 2.2
new stuff.

Of course, any console video should be built into the kernel, and not as a
module!

Jeremiah Cornelius

