You probably need to rebuild your kernel and include SCSI Tape support.
It is not included in the RedHat distributed kernels...

When you build the new kernel and reboot your system with it, you should
end up with a st0 device.

You can then use the dump and restore utilities to back up your system.
For my DEC TLZ06 DAT tape trnsport I use the following command lines:

        dump 0usfd 6600 .dev.nst0 42500 /
        dump 0usfd 6600 .dev.nst0 42500 /root/projects
        dump 0usfd 6600 .dev.nst0 42500 /home/segrest

Note that you have to dump each disk partition individualy.

Your milage may vary.....

Bob Segrest


