those lines.

You might want to check out http://www.redhat.com which is a company
that makes and distribute their own "version" of Linux.  If you go to
their online ordering section, look into "RedHat Linux Variety Pack", it
comes with the Alpha version of RedHat Linux.  It's only $30 US,
although I don't know if they ship overseas, but at that price, you
might be able to buy it out of your own money (although I don't know
what the Polish-US exchange rate is...)

Also check out http://www.redhat.com/mirrors.html for FTP sites where
you can download it from.  You can get the necessary boot disks (three
in all: boot.img, supp.img and resuce.img) from one of those FTP sites.

Also look into: http://www.linux.org for more general Linux info,
including HTML's and FAQs.

