wrote:

>Last week I had exactly the same problems when I tried to install
>rh5.2 on my alpha PC from Vobis. Sorry can't give a solution because I
>finally gave up. I asked on the axp-list mailing list, and the only
>hints I got were,
<snip>
>Again and again people write about "random freezes" during rh5.2
>installation. I want to stress that *my* freezes are *not* randomly.
>Freezes always occur at the same point, i.e. during installation of
>the rh5.2 glibc rpm.

Have you tried switching to one of the alternate consoles
to monitor the progress messages? ALT-F4 I think.

Is it possible that you are having disk errors? A similar
problem was bugging me while trying to install 5.2 on a noname.
First it died with sig11. Getting the new ramdisk fixed that.
Then, while compiling a new kernel, it would always die, at the
same spot, while doing a 'make dep'. It turns out that the
termination resistors had worked their way loose and whatever
sequence of disk commands were happening at that point would
guarantee a "device not ready", and "unknown error"(those were
the last messages that I got to see before the drive spun down
and everything collapsed. Pushing the resistor packs back in
resolved it.




