DEC insiders (whose names I would not tell) are saying that the prospect
of having the DIGITAL compiler for Alpha/Linux looks promising.  However,
I heard the same story for longer than two months.  What kind of a tortoise is
Digipaq?

Recently, I ordered a P-2 400MHz and the Absoft f95 for Intel/Linux compiler.
I know that it is just slightly slower than g77 for Alpha-21164-533MHz/Linux on
average.  However, I had to tweak all sorts of things (such as libffm.a and
BLAS) to get the performance out of Alpha 533.  I decided not to buy a new
Alpha-21164-633MHz this time although the price went down further.
When I bought Alpha-533MHz, there was P-2 at 300MHz only.

They (Digipaq) really don't know how serious it is not to have a
decent compiler for Alpha/Linux.  For example, a commercial
code must be compiled with a decent optimizing compiler to
achieve a good performance figure.

The number of the installed base of Digital Unix cannot be compared
to that of Solaris.  You will find a lot of difficulty finding commercial
software products for Digital Unix.

Go figure.

