Jacob Gladish wrote in message <36B24C42.EBB3DF77@psc.edu>...
>I got some code the is supposed to be able to transer MP3's up and down
>from the diamond rio. and it built fine on a linux/intel box, but when I
>try to build it on my alpha, I get undefined references to
>
>_inb(unsigned long) ...and
>_outb(unsigned char, unsigned long)
>
These two function calls map to the Intel Instruction of similar name.

_inb returns a byte read from a specified Intel I/O port
_outb writes a byte to a specified I/O port.

Since these calls are native to the Intel platform, I would suggest that you
look at rewriting the code that uses them in an alpha approved way.  I wish
I could help more

Marshall






