Brian Seo <brianseo@linkonline.net> wrote:
>Hi, I'm new at Alpha..this might sound dumb even..
>Can I install Windows 95/98 on Dec Alpha machine?
>


You can install Microsoft Windows NT on Alpha machines.
This will give you Microsoft's Internet Explorer browser,
but Netscape doesn't make a browser for NT Alpha anymore.
There are versions of MS C++, Excel, and Word for NT Alpha,
but in general, NT Alpha software is rare.

If you have an Alpha that can run the ARC console, you
can install and run Linux and NT on the same machine.
I have an Alphastation 4/233 with Debian Unix and NT 4,
but after installing NT I don't use it for much except
letting friends play Microsoft's pinball game.

---Alex




