If you can find the SRPM, building a binary for installation is easy.
"su" to root, download the SRPM, do "rpm -i foo.srpm" to install it
under /usr/src/redhat, do "rpm -bb /usr/src/redhat/SPECS/foo.spec" to
build the binary RPM, then do "rpm -Uvh
/usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha/foo.alpha.rpm" to install/upgrade.

