You can get the .tar.gz file and compile it and install it.
I don't recall compiling 1.2.26 being that difficult.

You can download it from here, for example:
ftp://ftp.rge.com/pub/security/ssh/

When you have the tar file,
run
tar zxf <tarfile>

It'll unpack into a directory, go into the dir, read the
README or INSTALL file, and follow the instructions.

It might be as simple as doing this, though:
configure
make
make install

where "make install" is run as root.

