If you have SRM, you should use aboot.  Your main problem is that you
probably partitioned your disk incorrectly.  When you partition your drive
you need to use a BSD disklabel, not the standard DOS type partition
scheme.  You also need to leave room for the aboot stuff, so start your
first partition on the second cylinder.  You should really look at the
