>fine, but still, ipfwadm comes up with this error:

I found a ref in dejanews on how to fix this. netinet/ip_fw.h apparently
defines byte and packet counters as 32-bit values, while they are 64-bit
on Alpha.  This is fixed in the debian alpha version; if you compile
ipfwadm yourself, first change the stuff in netinet/ip_fw.h before
compiling, and it should work.

>Any ideas? Anyone using this with a dec alphastation 200?

It's not related in any way to any specific alpha hardware.


