There seems to be a number of distinctly different 
clock problems with these 164 systems running Linux. 

My latest one had to do with upgrading to RedHat5.2, 
and noticing that, although my hardware clock was
correct at power-up, it was off by 3 weeks after booting
Linux. Both the system clock and hardware clock would
agree, and both would point to next month. 

Evidently my /etc/adjtime had gotten corrupted. At least, 
I know that when I reset it to "0.0 0 0.0" and did a
/sbin/clock -Aa, after setting both clocks to the correct
time, things got a lot better. 

Now I only need to fiddle with the first number to try to
get the accuracy to match my $10 wristwatch. 

At least it keeps good time. Under 5.0, I would lose system
time depending on how much CPU time I was using...huge
simulations would slow down the system clock. Doesn't seem
to be a problem anymore.



