Hi!

On Wed, 20 Jan 1999, Mark Charette wrote:

> I've loaded the RedHat V. 5.2 Alpha version of Linux on an Enorex pc164.
> Everything seems to be working fine except the 3Com card. Since I'm making
> the assumption that the Alpha kernel isn't modular (insmod sure doesn't
> work - since it's not even there), and that the card was built into the
> kernel (since it has Type 1 support), is there yet something else that needs
> to be done? The card shows up as IRQ 18 and IO 0x9000 in /proc/pci.

If it's REALLY 3c509, then the problem may be with the internal card
settings. Insert it into a Intel box, boot from floppy and check internal
settings with the program (3C509XCFG.EXE or something similar), which comes
with Etherdisk for this card. Etherdisk is a collection of
drivers/configuration programs for 3c509/3c509B and it is downloadable from
www.3com.com. Turn off stuff, like "Optimization for Windows", disable
internal modem (whatever it is) and it may start to work. I had to do this
with my 3c509B on an Intel box, otherwise it didn't run under Linux.

Hope it helps,

Jurij.

