For Linux on Alpha there are two motherboards currently in production. 
The first is the RX motherboard.  The RX is similar to the SX
motherboard except larger cache and faster CPU.  The RX uses the Alpha
BIOs

The second motherboard is the UX, designed by Deskstation, manufactured
by Samsung.  This uses the ARCs BIOs developed by Deskstation.  

The new motherboard that everyone is keeping their eyes on is the
264DP.  This is a dual processor enabled EV6 motherboard that requires a
custom case and 600 Watt power supply.  This baby is a beast!  And is
