    JG> "load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1" argument via SRM's aboot.

Here's the exact boot command I use to boot the installer:

BOOT DVA0 -FILE vmlinux.gz -FLAGS "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1"

You need to make certain you have the updated RAM disk image, or you
won't be able to select individual packages (the installer will
segfault if you try).  Check the errata sheet for the exact URL.

    JG> Since there's a "/live/vmlinux.gz" on the RedHat CD, I tried
    JG> doing a "boot svd100 -file /live/vmlinux.gz", but it doesn't
    JG> get very far...

I don't know what kind of device "svd100" is.  On my AlphaStation, the
CD-ROM drive is "DKA500".  In SRM, do a "sh dev" to get the exact list
of all detected SCSI devices.  The device that is your CD-ROM
controller should be pretty obvious.

If you're new to SRM, you probably want the SRM HOWTO.  There is no
Avanti-specific HOWTO (or mini-HOWTO).

