re -2.

    Do not overlap partitions. altough you can. Your bsd label must exactly
match your Partition table entries.  This is why you should use cylinder
numbers instead of blocks/sectors or bits.  if you do not use cylinders, and
you verify the partitions you will see it complain that the partitions do
not align with cylinder bounderies. The 2 cyliinder offset allows the bootlx
image to be written without overwriting any partitions.

JJ






