In article <77rf4u$do9$1@remarQ.com>,
  "JJ" <johnj@bicnet.net> wrote:
> Rob
>
> If you are going to use SRM and Aboot.
>
> 1. use fdisk, not "disk druid"
> 2. Create 3 partitions, use your own assignments, I just list mine for
> reference. But make sure you offset the first partition approx 2meg.
> (or 1-2 cylinders)
>
>         1st, partition offset approx 2Meg from start of disk.
>         I use 10meg partition 1 (Misc)  type - ext2
>         partition 2 remainder of disk -128 meg   (root)  type - ext2
>        partition 3  128 meg (type - swap)
> (Don't forget to set the type (filesystem type)
>
> Important!!!!!!!!!!
> Use Starting and Ending cylinders to define the partitions and record
> each partitions starting and ending cylinder number. you will need it later.
>
> After the installation is complete, reboot the system from the floppy
>
> boot dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda2"
>
> This will boot your floppy then mount your installed root.
>
> Log in as root.
>
> very carefully run fdisk on /dev/sda
> select b (bsd lables)
> print the exsisting  lable
> if one exsists delete all the entries.
> then create new partitions a,b and c using the starting and ending cylinder
> numbers you recorded during the install. with the same offset for the first
> partition.
>
> write the new label, then reboot as before to insure the new table is
> writted and read. (linux does not imediatly write) you can type "sync" to
> force a write, but I would still reboot.
>
> After the reboot, write your aboot label, It will work fine. I've done this
> several times this week on as800, 1200 and 4100 Alpha Servers.
>
> JJ
