Hi.

  Maybe someone can clarify this for me, but I was trying to recompile the
2.0.36 Kernel for a UDB Multia and attempted to include the TGA and VGA
drivers into it, when I did this, I got the error:  Invalied Reference:
curr_cons  in file tga.c  or something to that effect.  So I poked around
and compared the 2.0.36 Kernel to the 2.0.30 Kernel to find out what was
going on.  I found several issues that I don't understand:

The variable curr_cons  is NOT defined anywhere in 2.0.36 but is used
liberally  in 2.0.30.  Plus all the places where curr_cons is used, has been
"obsoleted" and replaced with a different format in the newer kernel.  It
appears the the tga driver was revamped somewhere between .30 and .36, and
in the process someone attempted to use the old driver for the newer kernel.
Could someone please shed some light into what happened and how to fix it?

In addition, this may be a completely different issue, but when I attempt to
use the 2.0.36 kernel (after commenting out the curr_cons line) I try to
boot and get a blank screen, there is some disk activity, and if I press
crtl+alt+del it appears to do a reboot, but I don't have any connectivity to
the box.
Thanks.
--
Danny Chen
Linux/Windows Programmer
