Danny Chen (dchen@csus.edu) wrote:
: The variable curr_cons  is NOT defined anywhere in 2.0.36 but is used
: liberally  in 2.0.30.  Plus all the places where curr_cons is used, has been
: "obsoleted" and replaced with a different format in the newer kernel.  It
: appears the the tga driver was revamped somewhere between .30 and .36, and
: in the process someone attempted to use the old driver for the newer kernel.
: Could someone please shed some light into what happened and how to fix it?

I would guess you got a hosed kernel source. curr_cons *is* defined in
./drivers/char/console_table.h in 2.0.36 kernel. It is also used quite
extensively throughout the source, albeit using indirect definitions
provided by ./drivers/char/console.h

Try getting clean kernel source, and start afresh.

/Serge.P



