Robert Miller wrote:

> Hi
>     I just finished loading redhat5.2 on my as200. Now I'm having problems
> booting linux. SRM comes up, I have tried booting the dka0
> it says no boot block found. I choose to install the workstation option.
> Do I need to install MILO? or is there an easy way to get ARC on the box.

You should install MILO in a small partition and then write:

    boot dkaXXX

From the MILO prompt you can, among other things,  inform the kernel about
how much memory you have. For instance, in my case, I have 128Mb  against
32 seen by default, so, after booting with MILO I write:

    set MEMORY_SIZE 128

and then

    boot ...

In some machines it is possible to load the ARC firmware or even the
AlphaBIOS. You may find more information at:

    ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha

--
Carlos Vidal
