Good news: The drivers work! I have a standard WinTV running in my 164SX and
formerly in my AXPpci33.

: I want to write out to a motion jpeg and share with editing systems.  I
: am hoping the alpha will be able to grab 30fps@640x480x16bit.
: This comes out to 17.578125 Mbytes/second?  Can PCI even support that?
I do not think that you will get this framerate on _any_ system. The most
limiting factor is harddisk bandwidth. Second the process of getting a frame
as data, not displayed on X11, is also CPU intensive. Third the on-the-fly
JPEG compression is nearly impossible at that speed.
A friend of mine tried grabbing with a BT848 card on two striped IDE
harddisks using UDMA with quite good success. The harddisk bandwidth using
diskstriping is very good ;) Maybe three harddisks get even better
performance.

: Anyhow, worth a try!
: Roger
