>	Hi 
>
>We are a small dev. unit and wish to buy a Linux alpha ( two
>in fact ).
>I think I will buy a Samsung 164-UX2 motherboard and a Proc
>Alpha 21164a 533 Mhz and a Red Hat 5.2 .
>We don't do images processing neither 3D.
>We'll be maybe 3 persons using gdb, gcc  and stuff like that
>on a single computer.
>
>I would like to know what is the amount of memory I should buy
>for this usage ?

The UX should easily handle that kind of a load.  You'll want at least
32 MB/user, probably more.  GCC takes under 10 MB to compile most
programs (although the linker can be a bit of a pig when linking big
programs like mozilla).  Emacs sits around 20 MB most of the time.
Any unused memory will be used as disk cache.  I'd imagine that 128 MB
is reasonable for 3 users in most situations.  (I don't know if you
can get 96 MB on a UX.  Maybe with 2x32 and 2x16?)

If you will be running many X clients on this machine, you may need to
adjust the above estimate accordingly.

-andy



