[This followup was posted to comp.os.linux.alpha and a copy was sent to 
the cited author.]

from the milo prompt get a directory listing of the kernel floppy:

MILO> ls fd0

Then boot the kernel by name:

MILO> boot fd0:linux root=/dev/fd0 rw load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1 
ramdisk_size=5120

I threw in the 'rw' and the 'ramdisk_size=5120' because I needed these at 
one point to get around failures. You may not need them.

Good luck.
- Peter Mott



