It appears that  "aboot" requires the disk be partitioned with BSD labels,
using minlabel.  However, 5.1 and 5.2 will not install using BSD labels,
complains about no-swap, and cannot set mount points.
or partition table corrupt. (disk druid)

I was able to install with 4.2  install aboot, then update to 5.1 (then
install errata's) and am able to boot from my scsi drive.

with SRM I
set os_flags "root=/dev/sda2"
set boot_file "2/vmlinux.gz"

then
boot dka100

otherwise

boot dka100 -fi 2/vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda2"

substitute your partition numbers
my root partition is partition2, swap is partition3
partition1 is offset ~6M from the start of the disk and I use it as
workspace.

my disk is
|---6M----|---10M partition a --|--200M partition b--|--60M partition c-|
^ aboot^       scratch ext2             root ext2                      swap

JJ

