Try using Micorsoft Sound System drivers: I/O base 530, IRQ 9, DMA 3.
check out: http://www.brouhaha.com/~eric/computers/udb.html
       or: http://www.alphalinux.org/docs/udb-multia.html
these are Linux specific sites, but may have helpful info.
 
> 2- Does anyone know if I can upgrade from the current 330 MB disk to a
>    4 or 6 GB one (what to buy, cautions ...)
> 
> 3- How to upgrade to 64 or 128 MB of memory (what type of Simms,
>    are they standard memories ...) ?

The Multia requires TRUE PARITY 72pin SIMM's, in banks of two simm's to
a 
bank. So just make sure you get two simm's & that they are true parity,
not 
just logical parity.
BTW, if you are upgrading the hard drive, you might consider setting it
up 
to dual-boot, so that you can boot NT4 or Linux. It can do this quite
easily, 
I had mine setup that way at first, but later reclaimed the NT partition
for 
Linux because I found I was never booting NT. But think about setting up
to 
dual-boot, it's a nice option.
Reguards,
-diahedrial
 
