kenand@nbi.dk wrote:

> Is it possible to compile the kernel with the core dump disabled or limited to
> some max. amount?

Specify:

% ulimit -c 0

after login.

This will set the coredumpsize for all processes run until logout to 0,
which will do what you're asking.

[ You don't have to recompile the kernel for this ... Heck, it seems
  that "recompiling the kernel" is getting the same status for Linux
  as "rebooting" has for Windows - the cure of every illness ]

