Ken Andersen (kenand@nbi.dk) writes:
> [...big core dumps...]
> 
>Is it possible to compile the kernel with the core dump disabled or
>limited to some max. amount?

Your shell should be able to do this.  In tcsh:

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
corton.inria.fr-bla/2038 > unlimit coredumpsize
corton.inria.fr-bla/2039 > limit
cputime         unlimited
filesize        unlimited
datasize        unlimited
stacksize       8192 kbytes
coredumpsize    unlimited               <--
memoryuse       unlimited
descriptors     256 
memorylocked    unlimited
maxproc         256 
openfiles       256 
corton.inria.fr-bla/2040 > limit coredumpsize 100
corton.inria.fr-bla/2041 > limit
cputime         unlimited
filesize        unlimited
datasize        unlimited
stacksize       8192 kbytes
coredumpsize    100 kbytes              <--
memoryuse       unlimited
descriptors     256 
memorylocked    unlimited
maxproc         256 
openfiles       256 
corton.inria.fr-bla/2042 > limit coredumpsize 0
corton.inria.fr-bla/2043 > limit
cputime         unlimited
filesize        unlimited
datasize        unlimited
stacksize       8192 kbytes
coredumpsize    0 kbytes                <--
memoryuse       unlimited
descriptors     256 
memorylocked    unlimited
maxproc         256 
openfiles       256 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Some shells use "ulimit", "ulimit -c" and so on.

Bye,
  Rob.



