I have an AS 2100 4/275 system with one scsi drive 'sda'.  I have installed
RedHat 5.2.  The install went fine.   I have three partitions defined.
sda2, sda3 and sda4.  sda3 is the 'c', whole disk, partition.  sda2, or 'b',
is a 512MB swap partition that starts about 10MB into the disk and sda4, or
'd', is a 1.3 ext2 partition that spans from sda2 to almost the end of the
disk; this is the '/' filesystem.

The RedHat install directions state that aboot can be installed during the
installation on the second virtual console by executing:

chroot /mnt bash
swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx -f3

which I executed during the install and it appeared to work correctly (ie.
no errors).  After the install and reboot I entered at the SRM console:

boot dka0 -fi 4/vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda4"

After entering the above command I get the following sequence of messages:

valid boot block
...
boot strap code read in
...
jumping to bootstrap code
can't open osf_boot

halted CPU 0

halt code = 5
HALT instruction executed
PC = 20000030

This system did have OSF DEC UNIX on it before we installed Linux.  Did I
get the wrong aboot code installed?  It appears to find the aboot code, but
then it can't get past it!

Regards, Kirk
