> On a ppp connection under RH 5.1 I get connections up to 38K4. Above there
> is miscommunication between computer and modem (that should accept 115k2).
> 
> Anyone having a clue as to what could be wrong?
> 
> Ron
> 
Yes, see below. I use RH4.2AXP on a Multia.

Append e.g. in /etc/rc.local
#
# Allow 115200 Baud on the /dev/modem although only 38400 is specified
#
setserial /dev/modem spd_vhi
#

In the RH4.2 Modemsetup define speed to be 38400. In reality this gets
converted to 115200.

Peter




