Rubin <rubin@xs4all.nl> writes:

> Hi guys,
> 
> I've got this problem setting up a (weird?) innd config..
> 
> This is what I need to do:
> 
> 1. No external feeds from other newsgroup-servers.
> 2. Make my own newsgroups on this server, ie: carbon.music.chat or
> computers.unix.help or whatever.
> 
> Is it possible? I think so, but I'm a bit scared of these config files
> ;-) If somebody has some advice, please help me out (I allready posted
> this to comp.os.linux.networking, but nobody knew).

1. Read the man page for ctlinnd.
2. su to your news account or whatever account owns all the news stuff.
3. Do something like:
   news:~$ /usr/sbin/ctlinnd pause "creating new groups"
   news:~$ /usr/sbin/ctlinnd newgroup carbon.music.chat
   news:~$ /usr/sbin/ctlinnd newgroup computers.unix.help
   news:~$ /usr/sbin/ctlinnd newgroup another.private.group
4. Edit your newsfeeds (/etc/news/newsfeeds for RH) file so that you don't
   try to propogate your local groups to your "real" news server.
5. news:~$ /usr/sbin/ctlinnd reload newsfeeds "creating new groups"
   news:~$ /usr/sbin/ctlinnd go "creating new groups"




