If this is indeed the problem, then it is easy: just answer "YES" when
prompted for experimental options early in 'make config' - 53c8xx driver
is still experimental in RH 5.1, and you need this to get prompted for
it. Somehow, I do not think this is your problem however - even if you
do not include your SCSI driver the kernel should not hang. Which system
type do you specify in 'make config', and what are the contents of
/proc/cpuinfo when running generic kernel on your machine?

